# A2/A2.1/A2_07_clothes_shopping.letz
# Source: PDF slide decks "L4 (Part 1)/(Part 2) a21convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A2.1, Lektioun 4, second half).
# Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered pages, then every
# lemma verified against LOD (gender -> article).
# Grammar focus: adjective endings before a noun, which the deck states as a rule —
#   masculine -> -en   (e gréngen T-Shirt)
#   neuter    -> -t    (e wäisst Hiem)
#   feminine and plural -> no ending (eng blo Mutz)
# Only feminine/plural attributive adjectives are used inside @sentence blocks, since
# those are uninflected and stay assemblable from taught tiles.

@lesson A2.07 "Clothes Shopping"

# --- Clothes ---
@word d'Blus = the blouse
@word d'Box = the trousers
@word d'Jupe = the skirt
@word de Rack = the dress
@word de Mantel = the coat
@word d'Jackett = the jacket
@word d'Hiem = the shirt
@word de Kostüm = the men's suit
@word den Tailleur = the women's suit
@word de Sweatshirt = the sweatshirt
@word den Tricot = the jersey

# --- Shoes & accessories ---
@word de Schong = the shoe
@word d'Schong = the shoes
@word d'Sandal = the sandal
@word d'Sandalen = the sandals
@word de Stiwwel = the boot
@word d'Stiwwelen = the boots
@word d'Schlapp = the slipper
@word d'Turnschlappen = the trainers
@word d'Mutz = the woollen hat
@word d'Kap = the cap
@word d'Händsch = the glove
@word d'Posch = the handbag

# --- Fit & size ---
@word enk = tight
@word weit = loose
@word d'Gréisst = the size
@word d'Kabinn = the fitting room
@word bëlleg = cheap

# --- Verbs ---
@word sech undoen = to get dressed
@word unhunn = to be wearing
@word undoen = to put on
@word passen = to fit
@word goen = to suit
@word ausprobéieren = to try out
@word de Kleederbuttek = the clothes shop

